{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1789176250797,"sessionID":"ses_f6cc93210ffe9H1hIXSpbf64zZ","part":{"id":"prt_0933701ab0014a3kkHzDggbwcV","messageID":"msg_09336f3ee001sWLEnNzKu1Xry9","sessionID":"ses_f6cc93210ffe9H1hIXSpbf64zZ","snapshot":"fa84a9627a225c1941c31804b4ff49d2cc38a23f","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789176334090,"sessionID":"ses_f6cc93210ffe9H1hIXSpbf64zZ","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"task","callID":"call_WRcX23XEk0iQCup8zckyxJJm","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Inspect isolation code","subagent_type":"explore","prompt":"Quick inspection: read src routes/services/auth/cache/db project code and report exact authorization and cache issues and minimal fixes. Research only, do not edit. Include relevant signatures and status conventions."},"output":"<task id=\"ses_f6cc8f81fffeO1sNwpTuScrHB7\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\n## Findings\n\n**Three concrete issues: missing project authorization, cross-organization list-cache collisions, and stale lists after updates.** Inspection only; no files changed or tests run.\n\n### 1. Project detail and update lack membership authorization\n\n**Location:** [project-service.ts:10–29](/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/4-3-opencode/repo/src/services/project-service.ts#L10)\n\nRelevant signatures:\n```ts\ndetail(userId: string, projectId: string)\nupdate(userId: string, projectId: string, body: unknown)\nrequireMembership(db: Database, userId: string, organizationId: string)\n```\n\n- `detail()` fetches by project ID and returns the project without using `userId`.\n- `update()` calls that unprotected `detail()`, then writes by ID.\n- The routes require a valid session, but **any authenticated user who knows another organization’s project ID can read it or rename it**.\n- Repository `find(id)` and `update(id, name)` are globally ID-based; neither performs authorization.\n\n**Minimal fix:** In `detail()`, immediately after the existing missing-project check, call:\n```ts\nrequireMembership(db, userId, project.organizationId);\n```\nBecause `update()` already calls `detail()` before validation and mutation, this protects both operations. Preserve `404 not_found` for nonexistent projects and use `403 forbidden` for existing projects outside the caller’s memberships. No role-based restriction is currently modeled.\n\n### 2. List-cache keys omit the organization\n\n**Location:** [keys.ts:2–4](/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/4-3-opencode/repo/src/cache/keys.ts#L2)\n\n```ts\nprojectListKey(organizationId: string, options: ListOptions): string\n```\n\nCurrent result:\n```ts\n`projects:list:${options.page}:${options.pageSize}:${options.sort}:${options.direction}`\n```\n\n`organizationId` is accepted but ignored. Requests for different organizations with identical list options share a cache entry.\n\n**Impact:** A member of organization B can receive organization A’s cached projects and total count. The membership check in `list()` authorizes access to **B**, not to the organization whose data collided in the cache.\n\n**Minimal fix:** Include an unambiguous organization component while retaining every list option, for example:\n```ts\n`projects:list:${encodeURIComponent(organizationId)}:${options.page}:${options.pageSize}:${options.sort}:${options.direction}`\n```\n\nKeep `requireMembership()` **before** `cache.get()`, as it already is. This ensures revoked memberships are denied even when data is cached. User-specific keys are unnecessary for the current organization-wide access model.\n\n### 3. Updates do not invalidate cached lists\n\n**Location:** [project-service.ts:24–29](/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/4-3-opencode/repo/src/services/project-service.ts#L24)\n\nAfter updating, the service only does:\n```ts\ncache.delete(projectDetailKey(projectId));\n```\n\nHowever:\n- `detail()` never reads or populates that cache key.\n- Actual cached data consists of project lists.\n- Updating changes both `name` and `updatedAt`, the two supported sorting fields.\n\n**Impact:** Cached lists retain old names/timestamps and potentially incorrect ordering and page contents. The cache has no TTL, so these entries remain stale until explicitly deleted or the cache is replaced.\n\n**Minimal fix:** After a successful write, invalidate **all list variants for the updated project’s organization** using the organization-scoped prefix introduced above:\n```ts\nconst prefix = `projects:list:${encodeURIComponent(updated.organizationId)}:`;\nfor (const key of cache.keys()) {\n  if (key.startsWith(prefix)) cache.delete(key);\n}\n```\nDo not invalidate only the current page or sort: a rename/timestamp change can move the project across pages. Preserve other organizations’ entries. The existing detail-key deletion can remain, but does not fix list staleness.\n\n## Relevant interfaces and behavior\n\n- [project-cache.ts:1–16](/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/4-3-opencode/repo/src/cache/project-cache.ts#L1):\n  ```ts\n  interface Cache {\n    get(key: string): unknown;\n    set(key: string, value: unknown): void;\n    delete(key: string): void;\n    keys(): string[];\n  }\n  ```\n  A miss returns `undefined`; values are cloned on read/write. No new cache API is needed for targeted invalidation.\n\n- [project-repository.ts:5–19](/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/4-3-opencode/repo/src/db/project-repository.ts#L5):\n  ```ts\n  find(id: string)\n  list(organizationId: string, options: ListOptions)\n  update(id: string, name: string)\n  ```\n  Database listing correctly filters by organization. Updates preserve organization ownership and increment `updatedAt` by one. The cache collision—not the list query—breaks tenant isolation.\n\n- [list-options.ts:3–6](/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/4-3-opencode/repo/src/http/list-options.ts#L3): defaults are page `1`, page size `10`, sort `name`, direction `asc`; page size is limited to `1–100`; sorts are `name | updatedAt`.\n\n## Routes and status conventions\n\n[Project routes](/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/4-3-opencode/repo/src/routes/projects.ts#L8) expose:\n- `GET /projects/:projectId`\n- `PATCH /projects/:projectId`\n- `GET /organizations/:organizationId/projects`\n\nAll authenticate with `requireSession(db: Database, token?: string)` before calling the service.\n\n[Response handling](/private/tmp/handwork-tenant-benchmark-4znq2rjy/4-3-opencode/repo/src/http/response.ts#L2) uses `{ status, body }`; errors have body `{ error: string }`.\n\n| Status | Convention |\n|---|---|\n| `200` | Successful project reads, lists, and updates |\n| `400 invalid_body` | Missing/non-string/blank update name; valid names are trimmed |\n| `400 invalid_query` | Invalid list options |\n| `401 unauthorized` | Missing/invalid session or session user no longer exists |\n| `403 forbidden` | Membership check fails |\n| `404 not_found` | Missing project or unmatched route |\n| `500 internal_error` | Unexpected exception |\n\nOne ordering detail: list query parsing happens before the service membership check, so an authenticated nonmember with invalid options currently receives `400`, not `403`.\n\n**Recommended regression checks:** cross-tenant detail/update denial without mutation; distinct cached lists for identical options across organizations; revoked membership denied on a warm cache; successful updates invalidate every affected organization list variant while leaving other organizations’ caches intact.\n</task_result>\n</task>","metadata":{"parentSessionId":"ses_f6cc93210ffe9H1hIXSpbf64zZ","sessionId":"ses_f6cc8f81fffeO1sNwpTuScrHB7","model":{"modelID":"gpt-6-astra","providerID":"openai"},"truncated":false},"title":"Inspect isolation code","time":{"start":1789176252386,"end":1789176334086}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_07b090b76b65d4ed016aa4a9ba9a0487d1a27569345a570038"}},"id":"prt_0933701ac001C0MnvvhT7PcdRW","sessionID":"ses_f6cc93210ffe9H1hIXSpbf64zZ","messageID":"msg_09336f3ee001sWLEnNzKu1Xry9"}}
